# .repo-status -- the publish decision, where tooling can read it.
# Template: publish-status.example in repo-secret-scan. One of: never | maybe | not-yet | ready | public.

publish: public
reason:  public so people can make their boards from a web page; made public by the owner on 15 Oct 2026 (D103, T132)
review:  2026-10-15

# The blockers of 12 Oct 2026, and what cleared each on 15 Oct 2026:
# - "nothing is built yet": v0.1.0 was released on 12 Oct 2026, and the page has grown since (CHANGELOG.md).
# - the survey in docs/research names other designers' published models: it was read in full for anything
#   that must not be published on 12 Oct 2026 (docs/backlog.md, row skadis-standard), and names designers
#   only as the credited authors of the published models it cites.
# - the commit rewritten out of history on 12 Oct 2026 (A35) was never on GitHub: a fetch of its full SHA
#   from GitHub is refused ("not our ref"), while the same fetch of a commit GitHub has succeeds. The
#   Gitea copy stays private.
# And a full-history scan with repo-secret-scan: 43 of 43 commits, 120 of 120 pattern self-tests, no
# binary documents, every hit a test fixture or the public noreply identity.
